      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "About this workflow",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# SDXL · film texture that actually shows\n\nBy **Agustí Figueras** · github.com/AGUS-LAIAMEDIA/comfyui-workflows\n\nAnalog texture terms (grain, halation, chromatic aberration) do nothing at flat weight in a long SDXL prompt.\n\n- Weight them **1.3–1.4**. Above ~1.6 it reads as a filter.\n- Add a negative prompt for small cleanups.\n- 2nd KSampler at **denoise 0.3** polishes surfaces. It won't fix geometry (dial numbers, fingers): use ControlNet / inpainting for that.\n\n**Note:** stock ComfyUI reads `BREAK` as a plain word, not as a chunk separator. It stays in the prompt only because it was part of the run that made the preview. For real separation, encode the texture block in its own CLIP Text Encode and join both with **Conditioning (Concat)**."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
